{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1100680-colin-chapman-s-kiths-from-b-j-zanzibar-s-world-of-darkness","id":1100680,"title":"Colin Chapman's Kiths from B.J.Zanzibar's World of Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-05T19:51:34-07:00","id":1100680,"title":"Colin Chapman's Kiths from B.J.Zanzibar's World of Darkness","content":"<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">OK; I'm really digging deep on this one. Back in the late 90s \u2014 20 years ago \u2014 a White Wild fan set up an archive for g toWoD homebrew material. Quality varied drastically; but it was worth delving through it for the occasional gem. In particular, the Changeling section of the website has a ton of Kiths designed by one man, Colin Chapman:</div><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><a href=\"http://\u200bhttp://bjz-backup.droppages.com/archive/adhsidhe.html\" target=\"_blank\">Adh-Sidhe</a></li> <li><a href=\"http://bjz-backup.droppages.com/archive/bakhna_kith.html\" target=\"_blank\">Bakhna Rakhna</a></li> <li><a href=\"http://bjz-backup.droppages.com/archive/barbegazi.html\" target=\"_blank\">Barbeghazi</a></li> <li><a href=\"http://bjz-backup.droppages.com/archive/bean_sidhe_2.html\" target=\"_blank\">Bean-Sidhe</a></li> <li><a href=\"http://bjz-backup.droppages.com/archive/bendithymamau.html\" target=\"_blank\">Bendith y Mamau</a></li> <li><a href=\"http://bjz-backup.droppages.com/archive/centaur_kith.html\" target=\"_blank\">Centaur</a></li> <li><a href=\"http://bjz-backup.droppages.com/archive/djidjigargaly.html\" target=\"_blank\">Djidjigargaly</a></li> <li><a href=\"http://bjz-backup.droppages.com/archive/fatae_kith.html\" target=\"_blank\">Fatae</a></li> <li><a href=\"http://bjz-backup.droppages.com/archive/folletti_kith.html\" target=\"_blank\">Folletti</a></li> <li><a href=\"http://bjz-bac