engeyokai</a></li> <li><a href=\"http://bjz-backup.droppages.com/archive/kappa.html\" target=\"_blank\">Kappa</a></li> <li><a href=\"http://bjz-backup.droppages.com/archive/oni2_kith.html\" target=\"_blank\">Oni</a></li> <li><a href=\"http://bjz-backup.droppages.com/archive/tengu_kith.html\" target=\"_blank\">Tengu</a></li> </ul></li> <li><a href=\"http://bjz-backup.droppages.com/archive/spriggan2_kith.html\" target=\"_blank\">Spriggan</a></li> <li><a href=\"http://bjz-backup.droppages.com/archive/swanmaids.html\" target=\"_blank\">Swan Maid</a></li> <li><a href=\"http://bjz-backup.droppages.com/archive/tokolosh_kith.html\" target=\"_blank\">Tokolosh</a></li> <li><a href=\"http://bjz-backup.droppages.com/archive/vily_kith.html\" target=\"_blank\">Vily</a></li> </ol>Take it as inspiration for more Kiths, for new kinds of Gallain, for new Thallain, etc.<br /> <br /> Some of these are redundant with subsequent material: goblins have appeared as Thallain, IIRC; Hengeyokai and Tengu were co-opted by Werewolf (though I see no reason why Changeling fans can't reclaim them); Leprechauns have been replaced by Clurichauns; nymphs are now a type of Inanimae; I believe that pixies have been replaced by Piskies; likewise, I believe the Sei are now the Hsien (though I could be wrong); and Spriggans are now a kind of Thallain. That still leaves the cat majority of these as untapped potential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\